{"schema_version":1,"guid":"2ef274e0-4526-4329-aa66-9ea600191752","apple_collection_id":"1553736450","show":"AI LITERACY - A Podcast about Artificial Intelligence","titel":"#8 How a self-driving car learns how do drive with Saquib Sarfraz (Mercedes Benz-Daimler)","audio":{"url":"https://anchor.fm/s/4848d648/podcast/play/47259807/https%3A%2F%2Fd3ctxlq1ktw2nl.cloudfront.net%2Fstaging%2F2022-1-6%2F246432052-44100-2-4546af48af933.m4a","user_agent":"PodcastsAM/1.0 (+https://amapps.app)","groesse":34707063,"format":"m4a","geprueft_am":"2026-10-09T14:45:54+00:00"},"faehigkeiten":{"clips":false,"clips_aac":true,"clips_suche":false,"range":true,"kapitel":true,"dynamik":"unbestimmt","grund":"Dynamik weder belegt noch ausgeschlossen: keine Merkmale gefunden, aber eine unveraenderte Wiederholungsprobe beweist nichts; M4A: Ausschnitte nur als AAC-Bloecke (clips_aac) - eine App ohne ADTS-Umverpackung zeigt keine"},"einzeiler":"How computer vision and neural networks enable self-driving cars to perceive and navigate.","kurzfassung":"Dr. Saquib Sarfraz explains how computer vision and AI allow autonomous vehicles to perceive their environment and predict behavior. He discusses the foundational role of data collection, the inner workings of neural networks, and why full autonomy will take decades to arrive. The episode provides deep insights into the technological and practical hurdles of self-driving cars.","stichpunkte":["Computer vision has been actively researched since the 1990s, well before the modern deep learning boom.","Autonomous vehicles rely heavily on cameras, lidar, and radar to map surroundings and detect obstacles in 3D.","Every connected car on the road today continuously collects real-world driving data to improve AI performance.","Neural networks function through hierarchical layers of artificial filters that learn to recognize features like boundaries and shapes.","Observation and prediction form the core of both biological intelligence and machine learning in autonomous driving.","Intent prediction models help vehicles anticipate pedestrian movements and react accordingly.","The industry classifies automation into five distinct levels, with most current consumer vehicles operating at level two.","Infrastructure changes, insurance liabilities, and regulatory approvals will delay full level five autonomy for decades."],"kapitel":[{"titel":"Introduction and Background","start":4.82},{"titel":"From Early Computer Vision to Autonomous Vehicles","start":168.5},{"titel":"How Cars Perceive and Map the World","start":552.52},{"titel":"Deep Learning and Neural Networks Explained","start":959.68},{"titel":"Behavior Prediction and Intent","start":1434.86},{"titel":"Levels of Automation and Future Timeline","start":1613.62}],"clips":[{"hook":"What really drove the AI boom?","start":267.494,"ende":295.126,"laenge":27.63,"byte_start":4650825,"byte_ende":5092968,"bytes":442144,"range_header":"bytes=4650825-5092968","vorlauf_s":0.0696,"inhalt_start":267.563,"anker_sha256":"6fcc3a5fb28be6f8da4826c996601471d2b510b3cf7a34bf60d2674486483ff2","anker_ende_sha256":"ca40db85dd5b52d34275bcbbbafa10d2d18c97dfff42d988322241abc2057641","einblendung_ms":60,"text":"The surge in artificial intelligence popularity stems from the availability of massive computing power and large datasets over time, overcoming earlier hardware and software limitations.","aac":{"profil":2,"samplerate_index":4,"kanaele":2,"bloecke":[399,378,358,346,362,419,375,340,341,355,371,407,531,343,382,361,352,369,344,360,330,362,357,332,372,372,440,439,322,306,350,371,372,371,372,371,372,371,372,388,355,371,378,365,372,438,305,371,372,372,371,372,371,372,467,407,462,463,323,317,363,326,296,315,460,401,322,429,345,309,310,372,371,372,371,372,372,392,354,368,372,371,372,371,372,371,372,371,372,371,372,371,413,450,408,386,373,358,293,302,361,372,371,372,371,372,477,351,340,320,369,372,371,441,381,430,349,318,348,334,371,372,371,372,371,400,357,358,372,371,372,371,372,371,372,371,372,392,35